1
00:04:36,000 --> 00:04:42,000
Dragon's Claws is a action film directed by Joseph Kuo.

2
00:09:12,000 --> 00:09:18,000
A "Dragon Claw" master returns from Manchuria
where he became a traitor to China.

3
00:13:48,000 --> 00:13:54,000
He's after the coveted Dragon Claw Golden Tablet that
will force people to bow down to him.

4
00:18:24,000 --> 00:18:30,000
He challenges the Grand-master who has a checkered past of his own.

5
00:23:00,000 --> 00:23:06,000
The Grand-master happens to suffers from a terminal
chronic injury related to his evil past.

6
00:27:36,000 --> 00:27:42,000
The traitor kills the grand-master, causing his wife and son the go into hiding.

7
00:32:12,000 --> 00:32:18,000
The wife seems to really be the Dragon Claw master in the family
and she vows to train her son the kung fu secrets.

8
00:36:48,000 --> 00:36:54,000
The son finds that one of his friends has learned a strange
style of kung fu from a filthy medicine man.

9
00:41:24,000 --> 00:41:30,000
The son seeks him out to improve his kung fu and defeat the traitor.

10
00:46:00,000 --> 00:46:06,000
Lung Hsia, played by Lau Ga-Yung.

11
00:50:36,000 --> 00:50:42,000
Ling Ko Fung, played by Hwang Jang-Lee.

12
00:55:12,000 --> 00:55:18,000
Beggar Medicine man, played by Pak Sha-Lik.

13
00:59:48,000 --> 00:59:54,000
A Tsai, played by Hon Kwok-Choi.

14
01:04:24,000 --> 01:04:30,000
Red Monster, played by Chu Tit-Wo.

15
01:09:00,000 --> 01:09:06,000
Green Monster, played by Chan Lau.

16
01:13:36,000 --> 01:13:42,000
Dragon's Claws is a British dystopian science fiction comic book,
published by Marvel UK about the eponymous law enforcers.

17
01:18:12,000 --> 01:18:18,000
Dragon's Claws first appeared in Dragon's Claws #1 (June 1988),
and were created by Simon Furman and Geoff Senior.

18
01:22:48,000 --> 01:22:54,000
Before their career as law enforcers, the Claws had been "the greatest Game players in the world" - the Game was a violent team sport, immensely
popular and funded by the governing  World Development Council, who had used it to distract the population and reduce civil unrest.

19
01:27:24,000 --> 01:27:30,000
Many of the villains appearing in the series also have their roots in the Game.
